WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.920
I am exactly thirty miles away

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.720
from the intersection of Beverly Boulevard
and North La Cienega Boulevard

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.589
in downtown Los Angeles.

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:10.230
This is part of the boundary
of the studio zone,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.660
a thirty-mile circle that
sweeps through southern California,

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.570
and which explains why a lot of planets in
science fiction look kind of the same.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.500
See, if I were filming a movie and I asked
my cast and crew

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.759
to meet me here, outside the zone,

00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:26.699
I'd have to pay them for their time and mileage
getting to the location.

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:31.189
But if I just walk a few paces this way,
inside the studio zone,

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:36.320
then cast and crew get paid from when they
arrive here, from their call time.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.570
Filming inside the zone is significantly cheaper.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.500
The headquarters of pretty much all the movie
studios are inside the zone,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.080
and so are a lot of places that you'll have
seen in film and television.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.010
Griffith Park and Bronson Canyon
are well within the zone,

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.690
close to the centre of Hollywood,
so that's where Adam West's Batcave was,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.580
along with where the walls fell for
Captain Picard, and along with, well,

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.140
pretty much any American TV show that's ever
needed that sort of landscape.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:05.399
And Vasquez Rocks, which have been used in
so many TV shows, films and music videos

00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:08.750
that there is a separate
Wikipedia page just listing them,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.570
is conveniently twenty-nine miles from the
centre of the zone.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.909
If those rocks were slightly further away
from Hollywood, then who knows?

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.560
Perhaps Bill and Ted would have been killed
by their evil robot doubles somewhere else.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.969
Why thirty miles?

00:01:21.969 --> 00:01:22.969
Union rules.

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:25.950
Hollywood is a union town, and long ago,
it was negotiated

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.750
that thirty miles was "local"
and anything outside wasn't,

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.720
presumably after many, many disagreements
going back and forth

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.080
between union reps and the studios.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.950
Now, exceptions have been added over time:
the rules are complicated,

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.210
and I couldn't explain them all if I tried.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:42.509
Production coordinators generally have that job.

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:45.429
But in summary:
this thirty-mile zone, this TMZ,

00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:48.380
and yes, that's where the gossip site got
its name from,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.219
this border is why, sometimes, it looks like
the crew of the Enterprise

00:01:52.219 --> 00:01:56.739
are boldly going where quite a lot of people
have gone before.

